# RC player-prop width canary: does the RC read a 55 ADDPLAYER prop at the width we gave it?
# Each 55 sets a test prop, then prop 0 (nickname) = CAN<n> LAST. If the test prop's width is
# mis-read, the stream desyncs and the nickname is not CAN<n>. Read it from the RC player-list
# window with a screenshot diff:  canary.py OUT ref-lost.png ref-landed.png X0 Y0 X1 Y1
# (box over the player row's nickname cell; capture the two refs from shots 01 and 02 here).
# Player id {ID} defaults to 7; keep it off any id the server already assigned.
waitsession 120
wait c2s 2 30
sleep 4
shot 00-base
# reference "landed": nickname set cleanly, no test prop
mark ref-landed
s2c 55 s:{ID} str:acct c:20 str:"" c:0 str:CAN99 c:11 str:head0.png
sleep 1.5
shot 01-ref-landed
# reference "lost": a deliberately desyncing junk prop before the nickname
mark ref-lost
s2c 55 s:{ID} str:acct c:250 b:40 b:40 b:40 c:0 str:CAN99 c:11 str:head0.png
sleep 1.5
shot 02-ref-lost
# prop 81 (player-list category) read as one byte: canary should land
mark p81-1byte
s2c 55 s:{ID} str:acct c:81 c:1 c:0 str:CAN01 c:11 str:head0.png
sleep 1.5
shot 03-p81-1byte
# prop 36 (rating) read as i3: canary should land if width is 3
mark p36-i3
s2c 55 s:{ID} str:acct c:36 i3:768350 c:0 str:CAN02 c:11 str:head0.png
sleep 1.5
shot 04-p36-i3
# prop 20 (level) as a GSTRING: canary should land after the string
mark p20-str
s2c 55 s:{ID} str:acct c:20 str:onlinestartlocal.nw c:0 str:CAN03 c:11 str:head0.png
sleep 1.5
shot 05-p20-str
# prop 11 (head): length byte, head name; canary after
mark p11-head
s2c 55 s:{ID} str:acct c:11 str:head25.gif c:0 str:CAN04 c:11 str:head0.png
sleep 1.5
shot 06-p11-head
# unknown prop 82 with a one-byte value, then three-byte value: which width keeps sync?
mark p82-1byte
s2c 55 s:{ID} str:acct c:82 c:1 c:0 str:CAN05 c:11 str:head0.png
sleep 1.5
shot 07-p82-1byte
mark p82-3byte
s2c 55 s:{ID} str:acct c:82 i3:300000 c:0 str:CAN06 c:11 str:head0.png
sleep 1.5
shot 08-p82-3byte
sleep 2
shot 09-end
